<h1>Build a payment IVR with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">Initech is a fictional company whose billing line takes card payments by phone. Callers hear a menu, enter an invoice number, choose an amount, and pay with <code>&lt;Pay&gt;</code>. The whole line runs on four documents published on voiceml.org and your own Stripe account in test mode, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/verbs/pay/">&lt;Pay&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "hash" %}</span>
			<h3>A billing menu</h3>
			<p>Press 1 to pay an invoice, 2 for the account balance, 3 to dispute a missing TPS report, or 4 for management.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "list-check" %}</span>
			<h3>Invoice entry</h3>
			<p>The caller keys in an invoice number and hears it read back, digit by digit, with the balance due.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "tag" %}</span>
			<h3>A choice of amount</h3>
			<p>Pay the full $495.00 balance, or only the $45.00 TPS report processing surcharge.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "shield-check" %}</span>
			<h3>Card capture with &lt;Pay&gt;</h3>
			<p>Card number, expiration date, security code, and ZIP code, keyed on the phone&rsquo;s keypad and charged through your Stripe account. Your documents never see the card digits.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "printer-fill" %}</span>
			<h3>A truthful closing</h3>
			<p>The caller hears a closing message that holds whether the charge was approved or declined, followed by an update on the receipt printer.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
